  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XE">Remark <span data-tag="00XE">7.15.5</span>.</a> (Skip on first reading.) Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. A quasi-morphism of sites $f : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$ (see Remark <a href="/tag/00X8" data-tag="00X8">7.14.9</a>) gives rise to a morphism of topoi $f$ from $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$ to $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ exactly as in Lemma <a href="/tag/00XC" data-tag="00XC">7.15.2</a>. </p>
